DOCUMENT();
loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'MathObjects.pl', 'PGcourse.pl');
TEXT(beginproblem());
$showPartialCorrectAnswers = 0;
$prompt = <<'PROMPT_7DA2_1EAC';
<p>7da2_1eac</p> <p>Which one of the following statements is<strong> <span style="color: #127663;"><strong>TRUE</strong></span> </strong> concerning differences between <strong><span style="color: OrangeRed;"><strong><span style="color: OrangeRed;"><strong><span style="color: OrangeRed;"><strong><span style="color: OrangeRed;"><strong><span style="color: OrangeRed;"><strong><span style="color: OrangeRed;"><strong><span style="color: OrangeRed;"><strong><span style="color: OrangeRed;"><strong><span style="color: OrangeRed;"><strong><span style="color: OrangeRed;"><strong><span style="color: OrangeRed;"><strong><span style="color: OrangeRed;">RNA</span></strong></span></strong></span></strong></span></strong></span></strong></span></strong></span></strong></span></strong></span></strong></span></strong></span></strong></span></strong> and <strong><span style="color: MediumBlue;"><strong><span style="color: MediumBlue;"><strong><span style="color: MediumBlue;"><strong><span style="color: MediumBlue;"><strong><span style="color: MediumBlue;"><strong><span style="color: MediumBlue;"><strong><span style="color: MediumBlue;"><strong><span style="color: MediumBlue;"><strong><span style="color: MediumBlue;"><strong><span style="color: MediumBlue;"><strong><span style="color: MediumBlue;"><strong><span style="color: MediumBlue;">DNA</span></strong></span></strong></span></strong></span></strong></span></strong></span></strong></span></strong></span></strong></span></strong></span></strong></span></strong></span></strong>?</p>
PROMPT_7DA2_1EAC
loadMacros('parserRadioButtons.pl');
$choice_1 = <<'LITERAL_7DA2_1EAC_CHOICE_1';
double-stranded <strong><span style="color: MediumBlue;">DNA</span></strong> has major and minor grooves, double-stranded <strong><span style="color: OrangeRed;">RNA</span></strong> does not
LITERAL_7DA2_1EAC_CHOICE_1
$choice_2 = <<'LITERAL_7DA2_1EAC_CHOICE_2';
<strong><span style="color: MediumBlue;"><strong><span style="color: MediumBlue;">DNA</span></strong></span></strong> nucleotides are missing the 2&prime; hydroxide (-OH) group
LITERAL_7DA2_1EAC_CHOICE_2
$choice_3 = <<'LITERAL_7DA2_1EAC_CHOICE_3';
<strong><span style="color: OrangeRed;">RNA</span></strong> has a regular consistent structure, whereas <strong><span style="color: MediumBlue;">DNA</span></strong> adopts a wide variety of tertiary structures
LITERAL_7DA2_1EAC_CHOICE_3
$choice_4 = <<'LITERAL_7DA2_1EAC_CHOICE_4';
<strong><span style="color: MediumBlue;">DNA</span></strong> can form a double-stranded helix, but <strong><span style="color: OrangeRed;">RNA</span></strong> cannot
LITERAL_7DA2_1EAC_CHOICE_4
$choice_5 = <<'LITERAL_7DA2_1EAC_CHOICE_5';
double-stranded <strong><span style="color: OrangeRed;">RNA</span></strong> is mostly in the B-form helix, whereas double-stranded <strong><span style="color: MediumBlue;">DNA</span></strong> is mostly in the A-form helix
LITERAL_7DA2_1EAC_CHOICE_5
$correct_1 = <<'LITERAL_7DA2_1EAC_CORRECT_1';
<strong><span style="color: MediumBlue;"><strong><span style="color: MediumBlue;">DNA</span></strong></span></strong> nucleotides are missing the 2&prime; hydroxide (-OH) group
LITERAL_7DA2_1EAC_CORRECT_1
@choices = ($choice_1, $choice_2, $choice_3, $choice_4, $choice_5);
$answer = RadioButtons([@choices], $correct_1, labels => 'ABC', displayLabels => 1, randomize => 0, noindex => 1, separator => '<div style="margin-bottom: 0.7em;"></div>');
TEXT(MODES(HTML => $prompt, TeX => ''));
BEGIN_TEXT
\{$answer->buttons\}
END_TEXT
ANS($answer->cmp);

ENDDOCUMENT();
